{
  "baseRefName": "main",
  "body": "TIDELING adds an original 2.5D reef survival prototype with Blender-authored rigged assets, three growth stages, seven baseline species, swimming/dash, combo, predators and a three-minute run. A disabled Bluegold species is reserved for the cross-application proof.\n\nThe Blender driver previously lacked a game-ready export operation. `driver.blender.export.glb` now exports one explicit collection to a new GLB, validates collection dependencies, restores selection, refuses overwrite and returns a SHA-256 receipt. A dedicated hosted harness builds a new fish through the real broker and both drivers, transfers its artifact, enables its Godot resource and checks actual gameplay collisions.\n\nValidation completed on earlier branch revisions: Blender semantic CI and native GLB adapter checks; Godot import, 13 rules assertions, keyboard/dash/collision acceptance and exported portable Linux pack smoke. Hosted lifecycle and cross-app runs are in progress. Current game remains a development prototype: final art/movement review, merged-SHA evidence and public release are not claimed. One visual review item remains open: central foliage competes with the swimming corridor.\n",
